WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.819
The turning of the calendar means that Netflix
is clearing its library of old content and

00:00:04.819 --> 00:00:07.090
bringing in a truckload of fresh additions.

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:10.960
The streamer has announced an impressive slate
of movies and television shows that will be

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.000
new to Netflix throughout April 2020.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:18.480
Among the streamer's early dump of popular
previously released action titles are several

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:23.361
franchise entries, including all four installments
of the classic action hit Lethal Weapon, which

00:00:23.361 --> 00:00:24.900
shows up April 1st.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.840
Once you've got your fix of Mel Gibson and
Danny Glover's spit-fire chemistry, you might

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:33.130
want to try your hand at several other action
entries that are classics in their own right.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:37.690
Among them are the '90s video-game adaptation
Mortal Kombat on the 1st, and, for Quentin

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:43.500
Tarantino buffs, his bloody, Academy Award-winning
2013 feature Django Unchained, which arrives

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.500
on the 25th.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:49.760
You'll also be able to stream Angel Has Fallen,
the third entry in the so-so Fallen franchise.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:53.980
This installment follows agent Mike Banning,
played by Gerard Butler, after he's framed

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:56.699
for an assassination attempt on the U.S. president.

00:00:56.699 --> 00:01:01.219
If you've seen either of the other two Fallen
movies, you pretty much know what to expect.

00:01:01.219 --> 00:01:03.120
Look for that on April 4.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.830
Despite having several oldies but goodies
populating this month's list of action and

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:11.480
adventure releases, Netflix is clearly banking
on one new film to be its number one streaming

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:13.250
hit of spring 2020.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:17.391
That's the Joe and Anthony Russo-produced,
Chris Hemsworth-led film Extraction, which

00:01:17.391 --> 00:01:22.470
follows a fearless black market mercenary's
rescue of an imprisoned crime lord's son.

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:24.240
Look for that to drop on April 24th.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:29.380
The current quarantine may find you more reliant
than normal on your gadgets, something that's

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.300
sure to have you questioning your ongoing
relationship with your home's digital intelligence.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.720
“Why did the chicken cross the road?”

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.740
“I don't know that one, why?”

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.860
“Because humans are a fragile species who
have no idea what's coming next."

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:46.940
If the pandemic has you pondering how you
and your tech are going to get along trapped

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:50.300
inside your home together for the next few
months, consider watching these films from

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:52.540
some of science fiction's greatest minds.

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:56.750
If you haven't sat down for a Neo binge lately,
you can re-enter the simulation with all three

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:01.409
parts of the Wachowskis' game-changing Matrix
trilogy, or watch Tom Cruise as he attempts

00:02:01.409 --> 00:02:05.670
to survive a very flawed futuristic crime
technology in the Philip K. Dick-inspired

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:07.040
Minority Report.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.869
Look for those on the 1st of the month.

00:02:08.869 --> 00:02:14.030
And despite its lukewarm critical reception,
Battle: Los Angeles' extraterrestrial invaders

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:15.959
might be just the thing you're looking for.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.320
Look for that one on the 27th.

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:21.720
Netflix has a solid list of drama titles dropping
this month.

00:02:21.739 --> 00:02:25.689
For those looking to escape the now for the
good old days, Netflix has a handful of April

00:02:25.689 --> 00:02:27.409
additions right up your alley.

00:02:27.409 --> 00:02:31.930
On April 16th, consider distracting yourself
with the likes of Hollywood A-listers Josh

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:37.540
Brolin, George Clooney, and Scarlett Johansson
in Hail, Caesar! — the 2016 comedic mystery

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:42.689
drama that centers on fixer Eddie Mannix's
scramble to save kidnapped actor Baird Whitlock

00:02:42.689 --> 00:02:44.800
and his swords-and-sandals epic from certain
death.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:49.100
"Sure, good… good stuff."

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:54.640
There's also the music-infused Cadillac Records,
about the turbulent lives of 1940s musicians;

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:59.959
or the high-stakes drama Molly's Game, about
an aspiring Olympian who builds an underground

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.080
poker empire.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.600
Netflix also has a few darker April offerings,
including Robert DeNiro's wholly unsettling

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:10.780
turn as Travis Bickle in the iconic film Taxi
Driver, or Jesse Eisenberg's performance as

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:15.960
the only sometimes unsettling Mark Zuckerberg
in the Facebook origin story The Social Network.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:17.719
All of those drop on the 1st.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:23.200
Though March 19, 2020 marked this year's spring
solstice, it never really feels like the new

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.959
season until April 1.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:28.640
That makes it the perfect time to opt for
a movie that brightens — not dampens — your

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:29.080
day.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:33.560
These comedy titles coming to Netflix in April
2020 will make the job of cheering yourself

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.960
up by getting in a good laugh a lot easier.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:40.340
Ed Helms is helping lead the comedic charge
this month — first with his starring role

00:03:40.349 --> 00:03:45.319
as the uptight dentist Stu in The Hangover,
arriving April 1st, and then with his turn

00:03:45.319 --> 00:03:47.260
in an all-new Netflix original.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:51.809
Starring opposite Taraji P. Henson in Coffee
&amp; Kareem, Helms plays police officer James

00:03:51.809 --> 00:03:56.080
Coffee, whose relationship with Vanessa Manning
is being sabotaged by her 12-year-old son

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:56.640
Kareem.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:59.780
Things take a turn when the boy and Helms
must team-up to save her.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.370
Look for that on the 2nd.

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:05.440
In addition to a slew of comedy specials,
there's a Ryan Reynolds addition to the Netflix

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:10.379
library that may or may not win you over — though
it certainly delivers on the same one-of-a-kind

00:04:10.379 --> 00:04:13.040
comedic charm that made the actor a perfect
fit for Deadpool.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.450
"You son of a b---!”

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:16.340
“Samantha!

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.020
You’re here!

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:17.580
S---."

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:22.160
Just Friends is a Christmas comedy about a
high school nerd, played by Reynolds, who

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:26.180
tries to escape the friend zone of his lifelong
crush and best friend, and you can stream

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:27.530
it on the first of the month.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:31.620
For those looking for funnies in a different
comedic medium, stream Chris D'Elia's newest

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.500
stand-up comedy special No Pain on April 14th.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:39.740
Spring might signal brighter days ahead, but
that doesn't mean you still can't enjoy a

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.230
darker flick on Netflix.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:45.360
The streamer is offering a decent amount of
sinister fare in April 2020.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:50.120
From deadly siblings, roommates, and neighbors
to clowns and demons, Netflix's thriller and

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:53.720
horror offerings for April are frightfully
fantastic.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:57.280
Start the month with classics that go out
of this world for their chills like Killer

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:58.660
Klowns from Outer Space.

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:03.420
Or tackle your fears of being replaced with
The Roommate or 2017's The Killing of a Sacred

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:08.840
Deer on April 5th, which follows a cardiovascular
surgeon and his wife after their picture-perfect

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:13.770
suburban life is disrupted by a fatherless
teen who inserts himself into their lives.

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:18.720
End the month with a brand new Netflix original:
Dangerous Lies, a star-studded mystery thriller

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.900
starring Riverdale's Camila Mendes.

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:22.060
Look for that on the 30th.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:28.460
Disney, and Pixar have dominated the animation
field for years, while anime has largely remained

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:28.980
an offshore import.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:33.930
But with a wide range of highly popular releases
like Voltron: Legendary Defender, She-Ra,

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:39.550
Beastars, Castlevania, and Devilman Crybaby,
Netflix is drawing a future where it's a true

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:40.840
competitor in the genres.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:46.310
April 2020 library additions continue Netflix's
trend of offering subscribers a variety of

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:48.680
new and classic anime and animation.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:52.740
The month's most interesting include the original
series The Midnight Gospel, which follows

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:57.030
a so-called "spacecaster" looking for the
meaning of life across the galaxy.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:58.500
That's touching down on the 20th.

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:02.770
There's also the arrival of the film that
birthed minions mania, Despicable Me, on the

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:07.770
16th, as well as two chapters in the classic
Bleach anime franchise, Bleach: The Assault

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:08.900
and Bleach: The Bount.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:10.860
Both of those land on the 21st.

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:15.380
Pokémon fans can also check out the third
season of Pokémon the Series: Sun &amp; Moon,

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:17.980
subtitled Ultra Legends, on the first of the
month.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:23.280
April showers might see you confined to your
house even if common sense doesn't, and that

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:25.670
means you'll need much more than a cinematic
distraction.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:30.110
Good thing Netflix has a bunch of binge-worthy
television series hitting the streaming service

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.340
in April 2020.

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:36.590
Rick &amp; Morty fans who haven't caught one of
showrunner Dan Harmon's earliest gems, Community,

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:39.860
can load up the show when all six seasons
drop at the start of the month.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:43.810
The series follows a group of heartwarming
but oddball community college students who

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:47.860
try to survive their non-traditional post-secondary
education — and each other.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:55.900
"This show's gonna last three weeks.”

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:57.020
“Six seasons and a movie!"

00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:01.330
On the more dramatic side, expect to see new
seasons from the Ricky Gervais grief-centric

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:04.170
drama After Life appearing on the 24th.

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:07.020
You'll also be able to catch two new small-screen
originals.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:12.220
First up, on the 15th, is Outer Banks, a young
adult treasure-infused mystery about eight

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:16.420
teens who search for one's missing father
leads to a treasure map and a long-buried

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:17.060
secret.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:21.440
The second, Never Have I Ever, arrives on
the 27th and is a coming-of-age drama about

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:24.160
a modern first-generation Indian-American
teen.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.680
The series comes from the mind and life of
The Office alum Mindy Kaling.

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:33.020
While you're busy social distancing, you really
have no excuse not to get your money's worth

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:34.520
with that Netflix subscription.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:38.050
There's no worse feeling than opening up the
app on your streaming device of choice to

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:42.200
discover that classic flick you were finally
going to watch has departed from the rolls

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:43.280
without ceremony.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:46.770
If any of these features are on your Netflix
bucket list, it's time to get after them with

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:48.400
a renewed sense of urgency.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:54.230
On April 29, Nicholas Cage's family adventure
movie National Treasure is taking a bow.

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:58.900
The 2004 feature film from Walt Disney Pictures
was produced by Jerry Bruckheimer and stars

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:05.030
Cage alongside an all-star cast consisting
of Harvey Keitel, Sean Bean, Justin Bartha,

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:06.830
Chris Plummer, and Diane Kruger.

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:11.710
Cage plays historian and cryptologist Benjamin
Franklin Gates, a man on a quest to uncover

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:13.920
the lost treasure of the American Freemasons.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:17.960
It's basically The Da Vinci Code for the whole
family, which makes it the perfect bit of

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:21.180
escapism to help your clan get through these
troubled times.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:23.480
Then comes the real culling on April 30.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:28.150
At month's end, Netflix is saying goodbye
to more than 30 classic movies including The

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:32.500
Talented Mr. Ripley, True Grit, and Blade
Runner: The Final Cut.

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:34.391
Raining or not, you can shed a few tears over
those.

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:41.140
"All those moments will be lost in time."

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:45.900
Still putting off that Police Academy marathon
you've been planning since before the holidays?

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:49.900
Better get to it, because the entire film
series is on its way out at Netflix.

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:53.300
Didn't get your fill of Scorsese's mobster
schtick from The Irishman?

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:57.840
Well, hurry up and stream Goodfellas, because
the 1990 crime story is playing on borrowed

00:08:57.840 --> 00:08:58.460
time.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:02.780
Both Scream sequels are scheduled to follow
suit, as are other horror classics Rosemary's

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:06.960
Baby, Friday the 13th, and the '90s witch
romp The Craft.

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:11.700
If you haven't seen Fairuza Balk hamming it
up as a teenage wiccan gone to the dark side,

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:12.740
then you haven't lived.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.540
The beginning of spring is usually a time
when most of us turn off the TV, slip out

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:23.230
of our soft pants, and squeeze back into some
jeans to venture outside from our winter hibernation.

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:26.580
Unfortunately, this spring is going to be
a little... different.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:30.760
But maybe you're more of a binge-watcher than
a cinephile, so if cannonballing five seasons

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:35.130
of premium television is your preferred coping
mechanism, then Netflix has some good news

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:36.590
for you in the upcoming weeks.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:40.360
Comparatively few of the streamer's lauded
television series are heading for the exit

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:41.360
in April.

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:45.740
Early in the month, Netflix is saying sayonara
to American Odyssey season 1.

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:50.940
The 2015 thriller series that originally aired
on NBC was adapted from a U.K. series entitled

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:52.150
simply Odyssey.

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:57.430
The first and only season stars Anna Friel
and Peter Facinelli as U.S. military personnel

00:09:57.430 --> 00:10:02.350
embroiled in an international crisis when
a military team on a mission to Mali discovers

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:06.760
that an American company has been secretly
funding a violent group of Islamic extremists.

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:11.220
If you enjoy shows like Homeland and Jack
Ryan, American Odyssey just may be your cup

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:11.980
of tea.

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:15.800
Then, mid-month, all five seasons of Lost
Girl are getting, well, lost.

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:21.130
The Canadian series began airing on Syfy in
the U.S. beginning in 2012 after originally

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:23.310
debuting on Showcase in 2010.

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:27.779
It stars Anna Silk as Bo, a bisexual succubus
in the big city.

00:10:27.779 --> 00:10:32.060
Perfect for fans of Supernatural or The Vampire
Diaries — and with five seasons of demonic

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:36.100
content to binge before April 16, you'd better
get cracking ASAP.

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:38.990
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:43.120
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies and shows are coming soon.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:47.320
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

